Notes on the two `missing` calls:
- **Unit 5**: every candidate still fuses at least two of the five short imperative sentences on one line; none fully separates them while also fixing the `Print GC / stats.` column-wrap.
- **Unit 8**: every candidate keeps sentence 1 (`_Translate just...immediately_.`) fused to sentence 2 on the same line — none actually separates all four sentences. My repair leaves the two very long sentences (data-structures, replacing-the-front-end) unsplit since neither has a real clause boundary (no qualifying `and/but/so`, and the only `that` would sever the subject from its verb), but splits the last sentence at `but`, which does join two independent clauses.
